  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Job Site You Finish Yourself",
    "overview": "The whole system is lifted from one photo the client posted: a fresh broom-finished concrete walk beside a rose-granite block retaining wall, wooden form boards, safety-yellow curb stops and a blue chalk line. Every surface maps to one of those materials. The dark slate ground is the night side of the site, the pale grey-green paper is the mortar, rose granite trims and numbers things, safety yellow marks the things you can act on, and chalk blue outlines only the form you fill in. Nothing is decorative that isn't one of those materials.\n\nIt is a phone-first, single-column page that reads top to bottom like a job: promise, what we build, who we are, how it goes, the estimate form, the close. Density is low and blunt; headings are heavy uppercase system type, body is plain sentence case. Two living elements carry the craft: a wet-concrete slab under the hero that a steel trowel finishes (on its own, or under your finger in any direction), and courses of granite coping between sections and on top of the work photo that nudge under the pointer and settle back. The page is otherwise still.\n\nThe owner's house style (Ellie's pitch-site rules) shapes the frame: system font stack, no sticky bars, the phone number in the top-right corner and only there on the first screen, at most two buttons under the headline, accents on hover rather than at rest, and the Facebook link sitting directly under the work photo where a visitor wants to see more.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Materials, not decoration: slate, mortar, rose granite, safety yellow, chalk blue, concrete, wood.",
      "Heavy uppercase system-font headings over plain sentence-case body.",
      "Two living canvases (wet slab + trowel, granite coping); everything else static.",
      "Safety yellow means \"act here\"; chalk blue means \"you are filling in the form\".",
      "Phone-first: one column, 56px pill buttons, 44px minimum touch targets, tel: and sms: links as the primary actions."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Curb-Stop Rule",
        "body": "Safety yellow is a fill for primary actions and a response to hover or focus. Cues such as arrows sit neutral at rest and turn yellow only when the pointer or focus reaches them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Chalk-Line Rule",
        "body": "Chalk blue belongs to the form. Every control inside the form (fields, chips, the send button) shows a chalk-blue outline on hover and focus; nothing outside the form uses it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signage Rule",
        "body": "Headings are 900-weight uppercase with tight leading; body never goes uppercase and never goes above 21px.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Thumb Rule",
        "body": "Every interactive target is at least 44px tall; buttons are 56px, rows 64px, chips 46px, fields 54px.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Material Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Shadows belong to things with weight (a photo, a trowel, a stone block) and are tinted with slate, never black. Cards, buttons, and rows stay flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Living Material Rule",
        "body": "Motion only ever lives inside the materials (concrete, stone). Text, buttons and cards never animate beyond color transitions (0.15 to 0.2s) and the 1px press.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** take every new color from the job-site materials: slate, mortar, rose granite, safety yellow, chalk blue, concrete grey, form-board wood.",
      "**Do** keep safety yellow for primary fills and hover/focus responses; cues sit neutral at rest (The Curb-Stop Rule).",
      "**Do** outline every form control in chalk blue on hover and focus, and keep chalk blue inside the form (The Chalk-Line Rule).",
      "**Do** make service lists whole-row sms: links with one arrow cue each; only the arrow fills on hover.",
      "**Do** frame client photos in the world's own material, as the granite cap does on the work photo, and put the Facebook link directly under the work.",
      "**Do** keep every target at least 44px tall and match paired buttons in height and border.",
      "**Do** honor prefers-reduced-motion by freezing the living elements to a finished still."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add a sticky bottom bar, or a Call button under the hero headline; the phone number lives top-right in the header on the first screen.",
      "**Don't** put more than two buttons under the hero headline.",
      "**Don't** tint, outline or shadow a service row on hover.",
      "**Don't** use chalk blue outside the form, or yellow as the form's focus color.",
      "**Don't** add thin decorative highlight lines or hairline glints; depth comes from shading and slate-tinted soft shadows.",
      "**Don't** let either canvas run behind text; the slab sits below the hero copy and the coping sits between sections.",
      "**Don't** give UI cards or buttons drop shadows; only the photo, the trowel and the stone blocks cast them."
    ]
  }
}